    <item ident="gf7c9f8e6ea03249dd2da02c1992853de" title="Academic Honesty">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>true_false_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>4527,6341</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="byui tesol101"&gt;
&lt;div style="border: 6px solid #376070; padding: 5px;"&gt;
&lt;div style="float: right; color: #fae5c3; font-size: 26px; margin-left: 5px; padding: 5px; background-color: #286177;"&gt;Honor&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Academic Honesty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Students taking courses through BYU-Idaho are expected to follow BYU-Idaho's &lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.byui.edu/student-honor-office/ces-honor-code" target="_blank"&gt;Academic Honesty policy.&lt;/a&gt; This includes avoiding plagiarism, fabrication or falsification, cheating, academic misconduct, and unauthorized uploading or sharing. BYU-Idaho takes academic honesty seriously and violations of the Academic Honesty Policy may result in consequences up to and including suspension or expulsion from the university.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;I read the &lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.byui.edu/student-honor-office/ces-honor-code" target="_blank"&gt;Academic Honesty policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="4527">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">True</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="6341">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">False</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">4527</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
    <item ident="ge4b31500992fd3e257c6c623c4a76640" title="Academic Honesty">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>3401,354,4894,4703</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="byui tesol101"&gt;
&lt;div style="border: 6px solid #376070; padding: 5px;"&gt;
&lt;div style="float: right; color: #fae5c3; font-size: 26px; margin-left: 5px; padding: 5px; background-color: #286177;"&gt;Honor&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Academic Honesty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Students taking courses through BYU-Idaho are expected to follow BYU-Idaho's &lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.byui.edu/student-honor-office/ces-honor-code" target="_blank"&gt;Academic Honesty policy.&lt;/a&gt; This includes avoiding plagiarism, fabrication or falsification, cheating, academic misconduct, and unauthorized uploading or sharing. BYU-Idaho takes academic honesty seriously and violations of the Academic Honesty Policy may result in consequences up to and including suspension or expulsion from the university.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
Cody and Angie are both in TESOL 101 but in different sections. Cody needed to take Quiz 1, a timed open-note, open-book, but not an open-person test. Since he had been busy at his job and dating Angie, he did not finish reading the assigned chapters. He had planned on organizing his material prior to the test but needed to help his friend who was sick. Panicked, he called Angie who had already taken the quiz and asked her what questions were on the quiz.&amp;nbsp; Was this academically honest?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="3401">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Yes, it is academically honest. Cody made an attempt to study but was too busy to finish the study guides.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="354">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Yes. It is academically honest. It is important for students to help one another through difficult times.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="4894">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">No. It is not academically honest. Asking someone who has taken the test what was on it is academically dishonest.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="4703">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">No answer text provided.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">4894</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
    <item ident="gdc0442d9b95566054e1f978202d1a70e" title="Academic Honesty">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>true_false_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>4527,6341</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="byui tesol101"&gt;
&lt;div style="border: 6px solid #376070; padding: 5px;"&gt;
&lt;div style="float: right; color: #fae5c3; font-size: 26px; margin-left: 5px; padding: 5px; background-color: #286177;"&gt;Honor&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Academic Honesty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Students taking courses through BYU-Idaho are expected to follow BYU-Idaho's &lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.byui.edu/student-honor-office/ces-honor-code" target="_blank"&gt;Academic Honesty policy.&lt;/a&gt; This includes avoiding plagiarism, fabrication or falsification, cheating, academic misconduct, and unauthorized uploading or sharing. BYU-Idaho takes academic honesty seriously and violations of the Academic Honesty Policy may result in consequences up to and including suspension or expulsion from the university.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cody and Angie are both in TESOL 101 but in different sections. They both use their local church computer to complete the assignments for the course. Cody notices that on the computer they are both using, Angie has already completed an assignment he was just about to start. Cody decides to download Angie's work, put his name on it, and turn it in. Is what Cody did considered plagiarism?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="4527">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">True</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="6341">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">False</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">4527</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
    <item ident="gc3bee7499f0976a3dd5023ba20611af9" title="Assignment Expectations">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
